question:
You are trying to create an alias resource record set in Amazon Route 53 using the AWS CLI. You have the following configuration file:
```json
{
  "ChangeBatch": {
    "Changes": [
      {
        "Action": "CREATE",
        "ResourceRecordSet": {
          "Name": "a.domain.com",
          "Type": "A",
          "Alias": {
            "Name": "applicationenv.us-west-2.elasticbeanstalk.com",
            "ZoneId": "Z1H1FL5HABSF5"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```
You receive the following error message:
```
An error occurred (InvalidChangeBatch) when calling the ChangeResourceRecordSets operation: Tried to create an alias that targets applicationenv.us-west-2.elasticbeanstalk.com., type A in zone Z1H1FL5HABSF5, but the alias target name does not lie within the target zone.
```
What is the correct solution to resolve this error?

