To move an apex domain when the source and target distributions are in different AWS accounts, contact AWS Support to move an alternate domain name . Resolution Use the AssociateAlias API to move your CNAME Note : If you receive errors when running AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI) commands, make sure that you're using the most recent AWS CLI version . 1. In the AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) policy of the user or role that's making the API request, add the following resource-level permissions: Important : The IAM user or role that makes the request must have these resource-level permissions in both the source distribution and target distribution. {
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "CloudFrontCnameSwapSameAcc",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "cloudfront:GetDistribution",
        "cloudfront:ListConflictingAliases",
        "cloudfront:AssociateAlias",
        "cloudfront:UpdateDistribution"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:cloudfront::SourceAcccount:distribution/SourceDistroID",
        "arn:aws:cloudfront::TargetAccount:distribution/TargetDistroID"
      ]
    }
  ]
} Note: Replace SourceAcccount with the AWS account number of the source distribution. Replace SourceDistroID with the source distribution ID. Replace TargetAccountID with the AWS account number of the target distribution. Replace TargetDistroID with target distribution ID. 2. Identify the distribution with the conflicting CNAME.

